# Tailwind CSS v4 Guidelines

This project uses **Tailwind CSS v4** via the `@tailwindcss/vite` plugin. Configuration is CSS-first.

## Configuration & Setup

1. **No `tailwind.config.js`:** All modifications to colors, fonts, screens, shadows, and animations must be written directly inside your main CSS file (usually `src/index.css`) inside the `@theme` directive.
   ```css
   @import "tailwindcss";

   @theme {
     --color-primary-50: #f0fdf4;
     --color-primary-500: #22c55e;
     --font-sans: "Outfit", sans-serif;
     
     --animate-fade-in: fade-in 0.3s ease-out;
     @keyframes fade-in {
       from { opacity: 0; }
       to { opacity: 1; }
     }
   }
   ```
2. **Usage of CSS Variables:** Any variable defined in `@theme` is automatically available as a utility class (e.g. `bg-primary-500`, `font-sans`, `animate-fade-in`).
3. **Container Queries:** Tailwind v4 supports container queries natively. Use `@container` on parent containers and `cq-w-sm:` etc. on child elements for component-driven responsive layouts.

## Standard Directives

* **Tailwind Imports:** Always use `@import "tailwindcss";` at the top of your main CSS entry point.
* **Transition Classes:** Combine `transition-all`, `transition-colors`, or `transition-opacity` with `duration-200` and `ease-in-out` for fluid micro-animations.
* **Avoid Arbitrary Values:** Avoid spamming arbitrary styles (e.g. `bg-[#123456]`). Map custom variables inside `@theme` in `src/index.css` to keep the design system unified.
